DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((x^3))^(1/3)");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln(((cos(x))^3))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(((3, 10) U (-infinity, 19]) - ((-infinity, 19]))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("((-infinity, 19]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (3, 10)) U (-infinity, 19]");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(3, infinity) U (3, infinity) U (3, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(3, infinity) U ([1, 11])");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(3, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 11]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((3, infinity) U (3, infinity)))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`17/11+11.59`]? [_____]{Formula('13.1354545455')}
---

What is the value of [`14+7.99+15-11/4.65`]? [_____]{Formula('34.6244086022')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 11\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cap A \cap (B \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 3 < x < 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 19\}`]

Compute:
- [`(A \cup B) - (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`(B) \cap A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, 5, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 3, 9, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 3, -1, 0 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 5, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 5, 4>") . Compute("<3, -1, 0>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, -1, 0>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -1, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -1, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, 8, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 10, -7, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, -7, -4>") . Compute("<-10, 8, 7>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -7, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-10, 8, 7>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, -7, -4>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, -7, -4>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, -7, -4>") x Compute("<-10, 8, 7>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
